{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And to teach.</b> These are the rulings." "<b>All the statutes.</b> These are the midrashot." "<b>Which HaShem spoke.</b> These are the halakhot." "<b>By the hand of Moses.</b> This is Scripture. The Targum derives it — how do we know [the obligation] to teach? From ולהורת."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {3 "The phrase מניין תלמוד לומר ולהורת is rendered literally; it appears to mean that the Targum (or tradition) cites ולהורת as the prooftext for the obligation to teach."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:09.017011892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}